    "note": "BACK-EDGE TO PROVEME, AND THE REASON IS A DEFECT IN THIS VOYAGE, not in the code. The forward PROVEME crossing was emitted without `proven_by`, so the ticket claims proven-space with no instrument named — and the clearance gate read exactly that back: '[proof_named] the ticket has crossings and none carries proven_by'. `cairn test --hollow` then had nothing to run against a reverted build, which is Law 8's whole question left unasked. The grammar models the repair as a back-edge rather than an edit, because a journal is a record of truth (Law 7) and the honest shape of 'the evidence did not ride the crossing' is re-crossing with it, never rewriting the crossing that went without.",
