      "actor": "CC",
      "note": "The one inference door carries a tool-using conversation. Four changes in host.py: the chat payload carries `tools` ONLY when the request does (so every existing caller sends a byte-identical body); the answer lifts `tool_calls` out of the host's message (it was dropped, and a cache hit replays the answer, so what was dropped was dropped forever); validated_messages grew a SECOND CHECKABLE SHAPE for the two agent turns, each branch refusing its own malformations; and ollama_resolver took a `horizon` policy as a CONSTRUCTION keyword (host.EXPIRED) so the agent lane re-resolves without a request key that would fork the canonical cache. LIVE FIRED against hex.local: full two-turn loop on qwen2.5:7b, and the second turn through the ROUTED production door on qwen3-coder:30b. MEASURED FINDING, not a defect of this door: qwen3-coder:30b — the only model the shipped stack declares for chat — emits its tool calls as TEXT rather than structured tool_calls on ollama 0.30.11; qwen2.5:7b, llama3.2:3b and devstral-small-2:24b all return them structured. That belongs to the hermes_shim ticket, not here.",
